  "body": "`cued` in internal/redact/model.go (`modelFits`) treats a cue as any substring of the 40 bytes before a value the local model found. So \"tool_call\" or \"callback\" cues a phone (\"call\"), \"telemetry\" and \"hotel\" do too (\"tel\"), and \"monkey\" or \"keyboard\" cues a secret (\"key\").\n\n#3577 was this: a bare `\"timestamp\": 1792903687` in a tool result was masked as PHONE. The Unix-time half is fixed on its own: a 10- or 13-digit time starting with 1 is never a phone, cued or not. Any other bare number the model takes for a phone or an account still passes on such a cue.\n\nFix idea: a cue starts a word (and ends one, or ends at a camelCase/underscore join), so `tool_call` no longer counts, while `phone:`, `tel:`, `api_key`, `apiKey` and `手机` still do. A test should keep each of those and drop each of the false cues above.\n",
  "closed_by": null,
